# A hosted child's place with a `$` answer below a building `if` of the child, under a
# host that stands below a building `if` of its own block (Semantics ch. 4; ch. 9: a
# supplier answers a hosted place, its `$` answer the place's dynamic, asked by the place
# as built; ruling TC: places are counted as they are built, so the host's number and the
# place's are known once each `if` is built). With the host at the top of its block the
# program lowers (sem-ch09-host-dynamic-answer-below-building-if), and so does it with no
# `if` in the child. Reaches `PlaceNumber`'s refusal "a place that is read at its block's
# build ... after a building `match`, `if` or widget of several clauses" on prismc-r27.
# Written by Claude (t2, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Pad.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

tag Pad.Ask of Element $Text:
    name: Text

@Inner: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Inner loud:
    if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"loud")                                        # [0]
    $a <- Pad.Ask(name="ask")                                          # [1], or [0]
    Ui.Label($text=$"asked {$a}")                                      # [2], or [1]

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"outer")                                       # 0
    ignore <- @HostDocument (@Inner loud), \|p, e| match e:           # 1/[p], or 0/[p]
        Pad.Ask(name=n): @ $"yes {n}"
        otherwise: @Element e
